-### Embed an Image
-
-`add_image` takes the image bytes, or any object with a `.read()` method — not a file path. Open
-the file yourself, which keeps the library out of the business of guessing encodings and leaving
-handles open:
-
-```python
-import aspose.slides_foss as slides
-from aspose.slides_foss import ShapeType
-from aspose.slides_foss.export import SaveFormat
-
-with slides.Presentation() as prs:
-    with open("picture.png", "rb") as fh:
-        image = prs.images.add_image(fh)      # or add_image(fh.read())
-    prs.slides[0].shapes.add_picture_frame(ShapeType.RECTANGLE, 50, 50, 300, 200, image)
-    prs.save("picture.pptx", SaveFormat.PPTX)
-```
-
